WEBVTT

00:26.625 --> 00:28.416
Oh. Kotaro. Are you okay?

00:29.000 --> 00:30.250
Here. Water.

00:34.125 --> 00:35.541
-Futaba…
-Hm?

00:35.625 --> 00:40.083
Am I… Do you think I'm gonna die?

00:41.708 --> 00:42.875
Don't you worry.

00:43.666 --> 00:46.416
It's fine. My mother is praying
to the gods, all right?

01:06.125 --> 01:10.583
One, two, three, four.

01:11.416 --> 01:15.750
One, two, three, four.

01:16.250 --> 01:19.708
One, two, three,

01:20.625 --> 01:21.750
four.

01:24.041 --> 01:25.166
Futaba?

01:26.750 --> 01:27.833
What's the matter?

01:33.500 --> 01:34.708
Do you think…

01:36.500 --> 01:40.333
Will cholera really go away?

01:42.125 --> 01:43.916
Father is gone.

01:44.000 --> 01:46.666
People in town are dying
one after another.

01:49.833 --> 01:50.833
And yet,

01:51.750 --> 01:54.166
we're still here, praying to the gods.

01:55.250 --> 01:56.083
Futaba.

01:57.500 --> 02:00.916
In this world, everything
that happens is part of the gods' design.

02:01.000 --> 02:02.791
And for that reason,

02:02.875 --> 02:05.750
the best thing
we can do in the end is pray.

02:09.083 --> 02:11.625
Whether it's war, or disease,

02:11.708 --> 02:14.166
whatever comes our way,
if we keep praying,

02:14.250 --> 02:16.291
the gods will protect us.

02:17.625 --> 02:19.125
We have to believe.

02:24.416 --> 02:26.583
All right then. Shall we go make supper?

02:28.583 --> 02:29.541
Yes.

02:48.291 --> 02:50.458
What's wrong?

02:51.166 --> 02:54.041
Mother! Mother!

02:55.166 --> 02:56.541
Mother!

02:57.666 --> 02:58.750
Mother!

03:39.833 --> 03:42.208
What's wrong, Kokushu?

03:48.458 --> 03:50.291
You're not the ones I want!

03:50.916 --> 03:52.666
Let's go!

04:00.416 --> 04:01.416
Hurry!

04:13.625 --> 04:15.208
Run, Futaba! Go!

04:17.000 --> 04:20.166
Run!

04:47.583 --> 04:49.083
Draw your sword.

04:49.750 --> 04:51.958
That brat is off your hands now.

04:59.166 --> 05:00.583
Do it already.

05:01.833 --> 05:04.083
Are you bullshitting me?

05:10.458 --> 05:13.333
Gone soft, have you,
Kokushu the Manslayer?!

05:22.416 --> 05:24.750
How's your life been since then?

05:34.958 --> 05:37.583
Those bastards in power do what they want.

05:38.208 --> 05:41.083
They told us to fight and kill
when they needed us.

05:41.166 --> 05:44.708
But once they didn't,
they told us to throw our swords away.

05:45.208 --> 05:49.708
That's why I'm grateful to the person
who came up with this whole little race.

05:51.666 --> 05:54.708
Because it takes me back
to the good old days.

05:57.166 --> 05:59.916
So let us return to the way we were.

06:01.541 --> 06:02.375
Shall we?

06:04.750 --> 06:06.625
Draw it!

06:32.541 --> 06:34.000
That's it.

06:34.625 --> 06:37.750
This is what I expect
from Kokushu the Manslayer.

06:59.416 --> 07:01.583
What's wrong, Kokushu?

07:29.125 --> 07:30.416
That's more like it.

07:53.083 --> 07:54.833
What the hell are you doing?!

08:03.125 --> 08:04.583
Mister Shujiro!

08:14.000 --> 08:16.750
Kokushu, we're not done yet!

08:18.458 --> 08:19.291
Hyah!

08:48.416 --> 08:50.291
Saga, what happened?
Is everything all right?

08:52.458 --> 08:54.625
Here, get inside. Come on. Quickly.

09:05.500 --> 09:08.583
Well, I hope you can get some rest.

09:08.666 --> 09:10.291
Thanks for everything.

09:10.375 --> 09:12.583
It's nothing.
Just let me know if you need anything.

09:12.666 --> 09:14.666
Though it's impossible

09:15.291 --> 09:18.041
to ever repay you
for all that you've done.

09:20.125 --> 09:21.541
It was ages ago.

09:25.666 --> 09:27.458
Well, I'll leave you to it.

09:40.541 --> 09:42.666
So it wasn't rusted after all.

09:50.625 --> 09:52.291
You saved me out there.

09:52.916 --> 09:54.208
Thank you.

09:54.791 --> 09:58.708
And you too.
Thank you for saving my life, sir.

10:00.291 --> 10:03.916
I'll take you to the edge
of the Tokaido Road in the morning.

10:04.000 --> 10:06.375
After that, take off your tag and run.

10:11.041 --> 10:13.083
It's against the rules.

10:14.125 --> 10:16.333
Your life is more important
than rules, isn't it?

10:17.500 --> 10:19.958
-I'm not giving up, sir.
-I don't think you understand!

10:21.500 --> 10:22.875
A child cannot survive this.

10:22.958 --> 10:24.500
I can't afford to run away either!

10:27.083 --> 10:28.375
If I give up,

10:29.541 --> 10:31.625
countless lives will be lost.

10:38.666 --> 10:39.625
Cholera?

10:50.583 --> 10:51.625
Who is it?

10:51.708 --> 10:53.250
Calm down. It's just me.

10:53.333 --> 10:55.666
You know I've got no intention
of fighting you.

10:57.208 --> 10:58.666
What are you doing here?

10:58.750 --> 11:01.166
Hold on now.
Why don't we talk face-to-face?

11:02.500 --> 11:05.875
I'll even enter with my hands up.
Just don't stab me, all right?

11:11.916 --> 11:13.375
It's good to see you.

11:14.833 --> 11:16.333
What do you want?

11:16.416 --> 11:18.166
Put your sword down first, will ya?

11:20.500 --> 11:23.041
If I wanted to kill you,
I wouldn't come through the front door.

11:23.125 --> 11:24.333
Go on. You too, little miss.

11:30.083 --> 11:34.625
You're all edge
and no ease, Kokushu the Manslayer.

11:36.708 --> 11:38.500
How do you know that name anyway?

11:38.583 --> 11:41.083
That's not what matters right now, is it?

11:41.166 --> 11:44.541
I think what you really want to know is
what I'm doing in front of you.

11:47.166 --> 11:51.583
Well, the thing is I've come bearing
a fine deal for you today.

11:52.541 --> 11:53.750
What is it?

11:57.333 --> 11:59.750
How would you two like
to form an alliance?

12:02.000 --> 12:03.125
What do you mean?

12:04.166 --> 12:05.750
What are you planning?

12:07.541 --> 12:11.708
Well, I just think this Kodoku game is
a little too mysterious for my taste.

12:15.750 --> 12:19.416
What do they gain by making
trained swordsmen kill each other?

12:19.500 --> 12:21.583
Why would they make us travel to Tokyo?

12:23.916 --> 12:26.708
Are they even serious
about paying us the 100,000 yen?

12:28.416 --> 12:30.166
And who's organizing this?

12:31.250 --> 12:33.125
You've been wondering as well, right?

12:41.291 --> 12:42.333
I heard someone mention

12:42.416 --> 12:46.000
that a group of high-ranking officials
might be planning a hunt for swords.

12:46.083 --> 12:48.708
If that was the case, they should've
killed us at the temple, right?

12:48.791 --> 12:50.875
Why would they bother
making us do something like this?

12:51.791 --> 12:52.875
That's true.

12:53.375 --> 12:55.666
Rumor has it some are out for revenge.

12:55.750 --> 12:58.541
Survivors of the old shogunate
forces are seeking allies.

12:58.625 --> 13:00.333
Right. I've also heard

13:00.416 --> 13:04.000
that foreigners are trying
to spark a civil war to destroy Japan.

13:04.083 --> 13:06.666
Anyway, the truth is still unknown, right?

13:08.416 --> 13:11.166
We have no idea what the
organizers are planning,

13:13.041 --> 13:16.625
nor what they may throw
at us going forward.

13:17.416 --> 13:18.916
What we do know

13:19.916 --> 13:23.125
is that whoever's
behind this is seriously powerful.

13:24.375 --> 13:25.791
It would be wiser to work together.

13:25.875 --> 13:28.833
We have better chances
of gathering information as a group.

13:29.416 --> 13:31.375
The sooner we learn who they are,

13:31.458 --> 13:34.458
the closer we become to the 100,000 yen.

13:37.208 --> 13:41.291
Well, then.
Is that enough to satisfy your curiosity?

13:46.750 --> 13:50.291
How will everything be taken care of?
There won't be any issues, right?

13:51.208 --> 13:54.791
It'll be as it was by morning.
No one will suspect it.

13:54.875 --> 13:56.916
So, how many are left then?

13:57.000 --> 14:01.083
The current count of those
who have survived now stands at 128.

14:01.166 --> 14:04.750
That's more than I anticipated.

14:05.375 --> 14:08.833
As expected,
the samurai are as tenacious as ever.

14:08.916 --> 14:11.916
The stench of blood, though…
Quite remarkable, don't you think?

14:14.333 --> 14:17.833
The organizer will be joining you
in just a few minutes.

14:17.916 --> 14:19.583
In the meantime, please relax.

14:19.666 --> 14:22.416
Enjoy your stay,
and make yourselves at home.

14:31.958 --> 14:33.583
We just left Tenryuji Temple,

14:33.666 --> 14:38.166
and now we're going through Seki,
Chiryu, Hamamatsu, Shimada,

14:38.250 --> 14:40.458
Hakone and Shinagawa.

14:40.958 --> 14:42.583
I tallied the number of participants

14:42.666 --> 14:44.833
against the number
of tags required to proceed.

14:46.083 --> 14:49.958
So currently, there are 292 participants.

14:50.458 --> 14:53.750
And in order to pass through
the final checkpoint in Shinagawa,

14:53.833 --> 14:56.000
you must have 30 tags.

14:56.583 --> 14:58.333
So, what does that say?

15:02.416 --> 15:06.000
It's possible
that several people can make it to Tokyo.

15:07.375 --> 15:08.916
That is correct.

15:09.416 --> 15:12.208
The figures show that no more
than nine could reach Tokyo.

15:14.375 --> 15:15.500
However, we don't know

15:15.583 --> 15:18.041
if those nine people
will be splitting the reward,

15:18.125 --> 15:21.250
or if the organizers might have
something else in store.

15:21.333 --> 15:23.458
It all depends on their goal here.

15:23.541 --> 15:26.291
In any case, if the limit is nine,

15:26.375 --> 15:29.750
then the three of us heading
to Tokyo together should be fine, right?

15:30.416 --> 15:32.708
How's that? Not the worst idea ever.

15:37.041 --> 15:39.000
Why form an alliance with us?

15:41.583 --> 15:43.750
You are not cut
from the same cloth as the others,

15:43.833 --> 15:44.750
wouldn't you agree?

15:47.166 --> 15:48.041
Also,

15:48.666 --> 15:52.291
I know for a fact that you won't turn
on me as long as she's with you.

15:53.666 --> 15:57.333
What do you mean by that?
Do you mean you'll kill her if I do?

15:58.916 --> 15:59.875
You know that I would.

16:00.791 --> 16:03.041
Think of her as a hostage, if you will.

16:04.958 --> 16:07.583
Well, we'll see
if you end up drawing your sword

16:07.666 --> 16:09.750
against our very own
little miss after all.

16:15.375 --> 16:17.500
You don't have to decide right now.

16:17.583 --> 16:20.458
There's an inn
over in Yokkaichi called Uzuya.

16:21.333 --> 16:22.750
Three nights from now,

16:22.833 --> 16:25.208
meet me there
if you do decide you'll join forces.

16:28.250 --> 16:29.333
Oh.

16:29.416 --> 16:31.458
I have one more thing I'd like to say.

16:33.333 --> 16:35.750
It's not that you're unable to kill.

16:35.833 --> 16:37.375
You're just choosing not to.

16:39.458 --> 16:42.416
Once a manslayer, always a manslayer.

16:43.083 --> 16:44.875
You're nothing but a killer,

16:45.375 --> 16:46.875
Saga Kokushu.

16:49.583 --> 16:51.458
I look forward to your answer.

16:52.083 --> 16:52.916
Wait.

16:54.333 --> 16:56.083
Just tell me one thing.

16:58.000 --> 17:00.375
What was your reason
for joining this Kodoku?

17:02.791 --> 17:03.666
Well,

17:04.208 --> 17:05.875
I don't know, really.

17:08.416 --> 17:11.583
Maybe I just wanted to witness it,
see how it unfolds.

17:13.208 --> 17:15.458
The final days of the samurai, that is.

17:18.625 --> 17:19.541
Well,

17:19.625 --> 17:21.041
I'll be waiting for the good news.

17:29.208 --> 17:30.708
Try to get some sleep.

17:47.125 --> 17:48.125
Mother.

17:49.750 --> 17:51.000
Have some water.

17:58.416 --> 17:59.250
Futaba,

18:01.041 --> 18:02.833
I'm so sorry.

18:07.125 --> 18:09.416
It's all right. Let me handle things here.

18:13.250 --> 18:14.416
Please, ma'am.

18:14.500 --> 18:15.958
Please, sir.

18:16.541 --> 18:18.666
Please. Even a little will do.

18:18.750 --> 18:20.458
It's for the children. Save the children.

18:20.541 --> 18:23.291
No one has money to spare in this town.

18:27.583 --> 18:30.791
Please. Who in their right mind
would believe this nonsense?

18:30.875 --> 18:31.791
Smells like a lie.

18:31.875 --> 18:33.625
What? Is it money you're after?

18:33.708 --> 18:34.666
Yes.

18:34.750 --> 18:35.583
Here.

18:40.250 --> 18:45.708
HOKOKU NEWSPAPER
PARTICIPANTS WANTED

18:49.416 --> 18:51.250
Hey! No beggars allowed.

18:52.708 --> 18:54.625
Hey!

18:57.458 --> 18:58.791
Futaba,

19:00.083 --> 19:01.458
I feel sick.

19:02.666 --> 19:03.958
Don't worry.

19:04.500 --> 19:06.875
You're being protected
by the gods, all right?

19:08.250 --> 19:09.541
Keep fighting.

19:11.791 --> 19:13.000
Kotaro?

19:13.583 --> 19:14.750
Kotaro?

19:15.791 --> 19:16.625
Kotaro!

23:07.666 --> 23:08.708
The ritual dance?

23:13.583 --> 23:14.666
Yes.

23:16.041 --> 23:17.666
What were you praying for?

23:22.500 --> 23:24.458
That everyone might fulfill their lives

23:26.083 --> 23:28.208
and find solace beyond in heaven.

23:34.500 --> 23:36.541
I learned the dance from my mother.

23:38.458 --> 23:39.416
She

23:40.416 --> 23:43.208
took care of children
who had lost their parents.

23:45.291 --> 23:46.416
But now

23:47.500 --> 23:49.333
she's bedridden with cholera.

23:52.416 --> 23:54.708
Some people still remain
in our village, but

23:55.250 --> 23:57.666
they endure both disease and dire poverty.

24:03.666 --> 24:04.916
Shujiro-san.

24:06.833 --> 24:09.041
Don't you see how desperate I am to win?

24:11.208 --> 24:12.750
But I know that I'm weak.

24:14.125 --> 24:16.000
I can't survive this by myself.

24:20.750 --> 24:22.291
So I'm begging you, sir.

24:24.250 --> 24:26.541
Will you please take me
with you to the end?

24:30.750 --> 24:32.791
I'll do whatever I can.

24:32.875 --> 24:34.583
Even if, eventually…

24:36.458 --> 24:40.166
you find yourself
forced to draw your blade against me.

24:42.125 --> 24:44.791
Until then, I have to keep trying.

24:47.500 --> 24:48.708
Shujiro.

24:49.375 --> 24:50.958
It's all I ask, please!

25:04.916 --> 25:07.250
I have a family I want to save too.

25:12.708 --> 25:15.833
We'll get through this, Futaba.

25:23.041 --> 25:24.291
Thank you.

25:37.791 --> 25:39.375
I appreciate your help.

25:40.125 --> 25:42.583
Now here. Take these with you.

25:45.833 --> 25:48.250
It's all thanks to that sword of yours.

25:48.333 --> 25:50.416
It carved the path to a new era,

25:51.500 --> 25:54.916
one where people like us
finally have the chance to be safe.

25:55.791 --> 25:57.375
Nothing I have to offer you

25:57.458 --> 25:58.500
will ever be enough.

25:58.583 --> 26:00.541
Yahei, the times have changed.

26:04.250 --> 26:05.083
Take it.

26:10.833 --> 26:12.500
Thank you for everything.

26:12.583 --> 26:14.750
I wish you both the best of luck.

26:27.250 --> 26:31.250
HOME MINISTRY, TOKYO

26:38.833 --> 26:39.750
Come in.

26:45.000 --> 26:47.625
If you'll excuse me.
Apologies for the wait.

26:47.708 --> 26:50.041
Kawaji. Take a seat.

26:51.166 --> 26:53.708
Home Minister. What is your concern?

26:54.791 --> 26:55.875
Here you are, sir.

26:56.375 --> 26:58.083
HOKOKU NEWSPAPER
PARTICIPANTS WANTED

26:58.166 --> 27:00.875
We seized a few of these
in Tokyo City the other day.

27:02.083 --> 27:03.958
Yes, I've been informed of this.

27:04.541 --> 27:07.750
I wanted to investigate further
before reporting it to you, sir.

27:07.833 --> 27:10.541
In any case,
100,000 is quite an extraordinary amount.

27:10.625 --> 27:11.625
Indeed.

27:12.166 --> 27:14.458
Last night at Kyoto's Tenryuji Temple,

27:14.541 --> 27:17.708
a considerable number
of shizoku were observed assembling.

27:18.250 --> 27:20.458
We have not heard any news
from Ando Jinbe,

27:20.541 --> 27:22.208
who was sent to infiltrate their meeting.

27:22.291 --> 27:24.541
Do you think the shizoku are trying
to start a rebellion?

27:24.625 --> 27:27.166
We still do not know what their goal is.

27:27.250 --> 27:29.875
However, they are remnants of the samurai,

27:29.958 --> 27:32.625
so they're definitely stirring up
some scheme in Kyoto.

27:32.708 --> 27:33.958
And behind them,

27:34.041 --> 27:35.958
there's someone
with enough financial power

27:36.041 --> 27:39.166
to circulate forged newspapers
across the entire country.

27:39.666 --> 27:41.333
As of now, those are the facts.

27:42.541 --> 27:43.916
Should money fall into the hands

27:44.000 --> 27:45.625
of shizoku
resentful of the new government,

27:45.708 --> 27:46.958
the consequences could be dire.

27:47.041 --> 27:49.125
We have to investigate immediately.

27:49.208 --> 27:50.708
Mr. Maejima,

27:50.791 --> 27:52.875
I don't think we need
to be so afraid of them, sir.

27:52.958 --> 27:56.083
-The shizoku are toothless tigers now.
-Shouldn't underestimate their strength.

27:56.166 --> 27:59.708
Have you forgotten how badly we suffered
during last year's uprising?

28:01.250 --> 28:03.875
Our nation has only just risen
from the ashes.

28:04.875 --> 28:06.916
If civil war breaks out once more,

28:07.000 --> 28:09.000
our nation will surely be shaken,

28:09.083 --> 28:11.333
leaving us at the mercy of the West.

28:12.666 --> 28:13.541
Kawaji.

28:14.041 --> 28:16.208
Let us launch an investigation.

28:16.291 --> 28:19.916
As for the person who's behind this,
the mastermind and their intentions?

28:20.000 --> 28:22.791
-The Police Bureau will find them.
-Sir.

28:37.000 --> 28:38.500
Did you not hear me?

28:39.291 --> 28:43.250
Did you see a samurai passing
through here with a kid or not?

28:46.083 --> 28:47.291
It's no use, huh?

28:47.375 --> 28:50.375
Please have mercy! I beg you!

28:50.458 --> 28:51.875
Have mercy!

28:52.625 --> 28:53.458
You beast.

28:54.125 --> 28:56.416
Stop attacking non-participants.

29:01.625 --> 29:03.625
Never seen you before. Who are you?

29:03.708 --> 29:05.791
Kikuomi Ukyo.

29:05.875 --> 29:07.000
Oh.

29:07.083 --> 29:10.291
I see. You're the famous
Guardian of the Nobility.

29:10.916 --> 29:12.708
Seek shelter while you can.

29:12.791 --> 29:17.375
I've heard rumors. What a shame!

29:17.458 --> 29:18.875
To be tossed aside like that

29:18.958 --> 29:23.000
after all those years
of loyal service to your master.

29:24.375 --> 29:27.333
So it seems we're in the same boat
at the end of the day, are we not?

29:27.416 --> 29:28.625
Shut your mouth.

29:29.125 --> 29:31.416
You and I are nothing alike,
you vile scum.

29:35.916 --> 29:37.666
Let's have some fun.

30:47.416 --> 30:49.833
Prancing around
like a damn snake in the grass.

30:49.916 --> 30:50.750
Enough of that!

30:51.333 --> 30:53.416
What's wrong? Can't keep up with it?

31:12.291 --> 31:14.166
Shall we end this?

31:14.666 --> 31:15.958
Because frankly,

31:16.625 --> 31:19.458
my time is far too valuable
to waste on battling you.

31:27.750 --> 31:31.000
Mr. Ukyo! You cannot see Lord Kazanin!

31:31.625 --> 31:34.250
Mr. Ukyo!

31:36.416 --> 31:37.583
Lord Kazanin.

31:38.125 --> 31:41.083
Are you truly abandoning
the Kikuomi household?

31:41.166 --> 31:42.583
I'm eating now.

31:45.458 --> 31:48.041
Our house, the Kikuomi, have repeatedly

31:48.125 --> 31:50.916
risked life and limb
to protect your noble lives.

31:51.875 --> 31:53.875
And this is how you repay us?

31:53.958 --> 31:55.666
Without their swords,

31:55.750 --> 31:58.750
the samurai are not worth much
to the world anymore.

32:02.000 --> 32:04.750
The government took your wealth too,
I suppose.

32:04.833 --> 32:06.583
So if you bow your head and beg,

32:06.666 --> 32:08.750
I just might consider
hiring you as my servant.

32:11.666 --> 32:12.708
Miserable cur!

32:13.291 --> 32:14.416
Don't move!

32:14.500 --> 32:16.125
Take your hand off your sword!

32:22.875 --> 32:24.458
Get him out of here!

32:25.166 --> 32:26.583
Hands off!

32:28.625 --> 32:30.250
I'll walk out on my own.

32:34.250 --> 32:36.875
Lowborn fool with highborn airs.

32:43.416 --> 32:44.666
My Lord,

32:45.458 --> 32:46.750
we can go no further.

32:48.125 --> 32:50.166
We sold everything we could.

32:51.708 --> 32:52.666
The only thing left

32:54.208 --> 32:55.333
is this.

32:57.875 --> 32:59.791
They've taken our purpose from us.

33:00.500 --> 33:03.833
Now we're being driven
into selling our pride to survive.

33:06.916 --> 33:08.666
That is too much to bear.

33:11.416 --> 33:13.500
Committing seppuku and ending our lives

33:15.375 --> 33:17.666
is the only path to protect our pride.

33:21.750 --> 33:23.416
I have heard your thoughts.

33:25.416 --> 33:26.916
I understand your feelings.

33:29.041 --> 33:30.708
The Kikuomi family

33:31.916 --> 33:34.500
will have its glory restored,
I give you my word.

33:35.500 --> 33:37.166
We're with you, Lord Ukyo.

35:02.708 --> 35:03.583
Oh.

35:04.208 --> 35:05.541
You survived too, huh?

35:13.750 --> 35:16.000
-I have a favor to ask you.
-Don't come any closer.

35:16.083 --> 35:16.916
What?

35:18.375 --> 35:22.125
No, wait, wait, wait! No, no, don't!
We don't want to fight. We've had enough!

35:26.291 --> 35:28.958
Uh, we're going to quit this game!

35:29.041 --> 35:31.666
Stand with us, please. Join our cause!

35:32.666 --> 35:33.916
What are you saying?

35:36.416 --> 35:38.583
We were tricked into this thing! Right?

35:38.666 --> 35:39.666
-Yeah!
-That's right!

35:39.750 --> 35:41.875
-This game is absurd!
-They tricked us into this!

35:41.958 --> 35:45.750
We don't stand a chance.
Everyone else is too strong.

35:45.833 --> 35:49.166
And then they took all our tags we won,
the tags we risked our necks for!

35:50.416 --> 35:53.500
-I'm sure the prize money is a lie too!
-He's right.

35:55.208 --> 35:58.875
So please. Join us.

36:00.250 --> 36:01.708
I'm begging you.

36:02.416 --> 36:04.375
We need more people in our cause.

36:05.375 --> 36:07.416
You can't leave now. It's too late.

36:07.500 --> 36:09.583
They'll kill you
if you break the rules, you know that.

36:09.666 --> 36:10.666
No.

36:11.208 --> 36:12.750
They won't. Look!

36:12.833 --> 36:15.625
Even they wouldn't dare.
Not with all these people.

36:15.708 --> 36:16.666
Right?

36:19.750 --> 36:22.916
It's nonsense.
Why should we be killing each other?

36:26.875 --> 36:29.666
Over something as trivial as this?

36:31.291 --> 36:32.125
I…

36:33.083 --> 36:36.958
only wanted the chance
to earn some money, that's all!

36:39.500 --> 36:42.291
I only wanted my kids
to eat what they want

36:42.375 --> 36:44.791
-and have their fill for once, that's all!
-Don't.

36:46.500 --> 36:48.083
Don't do it. Stop it!

36:48.583 --> 36:50.375
They're watching.

36:51.041 --> 36:52.333
I wanna go home.

36:53.666 --> 36:55.250
Don't. Don't take it off!

36:55.833 --> 36:58.250
Don't! Stop it! Stop it!

37:25.958 --> 37:26.791
It's over.

37:36.708 --> 37:38.916
Shall we end this already?

38:15.916 --> 38:18.250
-Stop! Don't take it off.
-Please.

38:18.333 --> 38:20.625
-I just want to go home.
-Stop.

38:20.708 --> 38:22.291
Don't take it off. No, wait!

38:22.375 --> 38:23.625
Stop!

38:23.708 --> 38:25.625
Don't do it! Wait!

38:33.291 --> 38:34.416
I'm fine.

38:34.500 --> 38:36.791
Everything's all right!
It's fine. Take it off!

38:36.875 --> 38:38.500
We're okay!

38:39.916 --> 38:42.916
-Hey! Wait! Hey!
-The two of you can end this.

38:43.000 --> 38:44.208
Just take them off!

39:04.500 --> 39:06.375
Why?

39:07.833 --> 39:09.875
How cruel.

40:03.416 --> 40:06.375
Those who remove their wooden tags
will be duly punished.

40:06.875 --> 40:08.041
Do you understand the penalty?

40:43.541 --> 40:45.750
Sick cowards.

40:49.666 --> 40:53.041
You act like
you're some kind of gods, right?

40:58.541 --> 41:01.375
You think you can treat samurai like trash

41:02.958 --> 41:05.250
just because
you no longer have use for us?

41:12.333 --> 41:13.375
What was that?

42:38.291 --> 42:39.333
Sakura, sir,

42:40.041 --> 42:41.500
how shall we proceed?

42:43.750 --> 42:45.416
Let the organizer know.

42:46.500 --> 42:47.791
As you command.

42:56.166 --> 42:58.041
Kokushu the Manslayer.

42:58.541 --> 43:00.250
He has reawakened.

43:40.083 --> 43:41.291
This is…

43:43.958 --> 43:45.666
who I once was.

43:46.750 --> 43:47.750
What?

43:52.541 --> 43:55.208
All I knew was how to kill
and nothing else.

44:19.208 --> 44:20.166
Ugh.

44:20.708 --> 44:22.916
Ugh.

44:24.291 --> 44:27.500
That's it?

44:28.083 --> 44:29.541
No fun.

44:31.291 --> 44:32.625
There you go.

44:50.458 --> 44:53.333
117 REMAINING
